    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336-a2">

                <pb facs="0449" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg341"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Lord Stanley, of
                        Preston.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February 27,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With reference to my dispatch No. 2 of
                    the 3d ultimo, transmitting the reply of the U. S. Government to the last
                    communication of the Dominion Government respecting wrecking privileges in the
                    waters contiguous to the two countries, I have the honor to inclose an extract
                    from the Congressional Record of the 25th instant, in which it appears that the
                    Senate have agreed to an amendment in the act of Congress of June 19, 1878,
                    relating to wrecking in coterminous waters whereby the difficulty which has
                    arisen from the inclusion of the Welland Canal in that act will be removed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
